<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Margrave War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1552–1554</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Margrave War was a conflict of 1552 to 1554 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, in which Margrave Albert <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alcibiades">Alcibiades</a> of Brandenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulmbach">Kulmbach</a> plundered the bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a> and attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a>. An alliance of princes and Franconian powers, led by Maurice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, defeated him at Sievershausen in 1553, and Schweinfurt, which he had occupied, was destroyed in 1554.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-margrave-war.jpg" alt="Second Margrave War" width="320" height="254" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Friedrich Wilhelm Putzger (1849-1913). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deutschland_im_XVI._Jahrhundert_(Putzger).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
